Error Cause Fix <code>class file version 69.0</code> Java 25 required Use the <code>java25</code> image tag (MC 26+) <code>class file version 65.0</code> Java 21 required Use <code>java21</code> image tag <code>Unsupported class file major version</code> Java too high for Forge Use <code>java8</code> for Forge 1.16.5 and below Mods fail to load Version mismatch Check mod docs for Java requirements <p>Diagnosis: <pre><code>mcctl logs &lt;server&gt;
# Look for "class file version" or "Unsupported" errors
</code></pre></p> <p>Fix steps: 1. Check the Java version matrix in Section 10 (26.x / <code>LATEST</code>: Java 25; 1.20.5-1.21.x: Java 21; 1.17-1.20.4: Java 17; 1.16.5 and older: Java 8) 2. New servers get the tag for their <code>VERSION</code>; a server whose <code>VERSION</code> changed later keeps its image. Change <code>image</code> in <code>servers/&lt;name&gt;/server.yaml</code> and run <code>mcctl migrate spec &lt;name&gt;</code> (or edit the image in <code>servers/&lt;name&gt;/docker-compose.yml</code>; mcctl takes it into <code>server.yaml</code>), then <code>mcctl stop &lt;name&gt; &amp;&amp; mcctl start &lt;name&gt;</code> 3. <code>mcctl update</code> moves an unpinned <code>java*</code> tag to the one <code>VERSION</code> needs; a release-version tag (e.g. <code>2026.10.0-java21</code>) or digest is kept 4. For Forge 1.16.5 and below, you must use <code>java8</code></p>

Command Description <code>help</code> List all available commands <code>help &lt;command&gt;</code> Show usage for specific command <code>help &lt;page&gt;</code> Show help page (1-8) <pre><code>&gt; help tp
/tp &lt;destination&gt;
/tp &lt;location&gt;
/tp &lt;targets&gt; &lt;destination&gt;
/tp &lt;targets&gt; &lt;location&gt;
...
</code></pre>

Option 1: .mcctl.jsonOption 2: DO_NOT_TRACK <p>Add <code>"telemetry": false</code> to <code>&lt;root&gt;/.mcctl.json</code> and keep the existing fields. It takes effect from the next page load, and no restart is needed.</p> <pre><code>{
  "telemetry": false
}
</code></pre> <p>Set <code>DO_NOT_TRACK=1</code> in the mcctl-console <code>env</code> in PM2's <code>ecosystem.config.cjs</code>, then recreate the PM2 processes so they read the new <code>env</code>. A plain <code>mcctl console service restart</code> keeps the environment PM2 already has.</p> <pre><code>mcctl console service restart --console --force
</code></pre> <p><code>--force</code> kills the PM2 daemon, so other apps managed by PM2 stop as well (see <code>mcctl console service restart</code>). <code>mcctl console init --force</code> writes a new <code>ecosystem.config.cjs</code> without this setting.</p>

Piece File Use case <code>shared/src/application/use-cases/ConfigSnapshotUseCase.ts</code> Handlers <code>cli/src/commands/config-snapshot/{list,create,show,diff,restore,delete}.ts</code> and <code>schedule/</code> Container getter <code>configSnapshotUseCase</code> in <code>container.ts</code> Test <code>cli/tests/commands/config-snapshot.test.ts</code> <p>A handler is small: build the container, call the use case, print.</p> <pre><code>// cli/src/commands/config-snapshot/list.ts
export async function configSnapshotListCommand(
  options: ConfigSnapshotListOptions
): Promise&lt;number&gt; {
  const container = getContainer(options.root);
  const useCase = container.configSnapshotUseCase;
  const limit = options.limit ?? 20;

  try {
    const snapshots = await useCase.list(options.serverName, limit, options.offset);
    if (options.json) {
      console.log(JSON.stringify(snapshots.map((s) =&gt; s.toJSON()), null, 2));
      return 0;
    }
    // ... format and print
    return 0;
  } catch (error) {
    // log error
    return 1;
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>Dispatch in <code>cli/src/index.ts</code>:</p> <pre><code>case 'config-snapshot': {
  const csAction = subCommand;
  if (csAction === 'schedule') {
    const scheduleAction = positional[0];
    switch (scheduleAction) {
      case 'list':
        exitCode = await configSnapshotScheduleListCommand({
          root: rootDir,
          serverName: flags['server'] as string | undefined,
          json: flags['json'] === true,
        });
        break;
      // add, remove, enable, disable ...
    }
    break;
  }
  // list, create, show, diff, restore, delete ...
}
</code></pre>

명령어 설명 <code>help</code> 사용 가능한 모든 명령어 목록 <code>help &lt;명령어&gt;</code> 특정 명령어 사용법 표시 <code>help &lt;페이지&gt;</code> 도움말 페이지 표시 (1-8) <pre><code>&gt; help tp
/tp &lt;destination&gt;
/tp &lt;location&gt;
/tp &lt;targets&gt; &lt;destination&gt;
/tp &lt;targets&gt; &lt;location&gt;
...
</code></pre>

방법 1: .mcctl.json방법 2: DO_NOT_TRACK <p><code>&lt;root&gt;/.mcctl.json</code>의 기존 필드는 그대로 두고 <code>"telemetry": false</code>를 추가합니다. 다음 페이지 로드부터 적용되며 재시작은 필요 없습니다.</p> <pre><code>{
  "telemetry": false
}
</code></pre> <p>PM2 <code>ecosystem.config.cjs</code>의 mcctl-console <code>env</code>에 <code>DO_NOT_TRACK=1</code>을 추가한 뒤, 새 <code>env</code>를 읽도록 PM2 프로세스를 다시 만듭니다. 일반 <code>mcctl console service restart</code>는 PM2가 이미 가진 환경을 그대로 유지합니다.</p> <pre><code>mcctl console service restart --console --force
</code></pre> <p><code>--force</code>는 PM2 데몬을 종료하므로 PM2가 관리하는 다른 앱도 함께 중지됩니다(<code>mcctl console service restart</code> 참조). <code>mcctl console init --force</code>는 이 설정이 없는 새 <code>ecosystem.config.cjs</code>를 작성합니다.</p>

구성 요소 파일 유스케이스 <code>shared/src/application/use-cases/ConfigSnapshotUseCase.ts</code> 핸들러 <code>cli/src/commands/config-snapshot/{list,create,show,diff,restore,delete}.ts</code>, <code>schedule/</code> 컨테이너 getter <code>container.ts</code>의 <code>configSnapshotUseCase</code> 테스트 <code>cli/tests/commands/config-snapshot.test.ts</code> <p>핸들러는 작습니다. 컨테이너를 얻고, 유스케이스를 호출하고, 출력합니다.</p> <pre><code>// cli/src/commands/config-snapshot/list.ts
